<title>MEXICO: POLL - Monterrey, Mexico, business climate improves.</title>
<headline>POLL - Monterrey, Mexico, business climate improves.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The business climate in Mexico's northern industrial city of Monterrey improved during July, according to a Reuters survey of 10 Monterrey-based publicly traded companies.</p>
<p>Six of the 10 companies said the overall business climate improved from the previous month, while four said it was the same.</p>
<p>The survey asked the 10 companies whether their results improved, worsened or were the same in the following categories (responses in percentages):</p>
<p>INDICATOR			IMPROVED     STAYED     WORSENED</p>
<p>						     SAME</p>
<p>Production volume		50.0	  37.5	  12.5</p>
<p>Domestic sales		   50.0	  30.0	  20.0</p>
<p>Export sales		     37.5	  25.0	  37.5</p>
<p>Cash flow			  50.0	  30.0	  20.0</p>
<p>Finished product</p>
<p>    inventories		  22.2	  66.67	 11.13</p>
<p>Cost of goods sold and</p>
<p>    administrative expenses  50.0	  20.0	  30.0</p>
<p>Capital expenditures	   44.4	  55.6	   0.0</p>
<p>Capacity utilization rate    33.3	  55.6	  11.1</p>
<p>Earnings before IFC*	   30.0	  50.0	  20.0</p>
<p>Employment			 20.0	  80.0	   0.0</p>
<p>Financing access conditions  33.3	  66.7	   0.0</p>
<p>Business environment	   60.0	  40.0	   0.0</p>
<p>*Integrated financing cost.</p>
<p>((--Marlene Galvan, Monterrey bureau, +528 345-7677))</p>
